#. Description of the 'Header HTML' (HTML Editor) field in DocType 'Letter
#. Head'
#: frappe/printing/doctype/letter_head/letter_head.json
msgid "Letter Head in HTML"
msgstr ""
"A **letterhead** in HTML is the header section of a document that typically contains a company's branding elements such as logo, name, address, and contact information. It's commonly used in invoices, official letters, and reports.\n"
"\n"
"Here's a basic example:\n"
"\n"
"```html\n"
"<div class=\"letterhead\">\n"
"  <img src=\"logo.png\" alt=\"Company Logo\" />\n"
"  <h1>Company Name</h1>\n"
"  <p>123 Main St, City, State 12345</p>\n"
"  <p>Phone: (555) 123-4567 | Email: info@company.com</p>\n"
"</div>\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"In ERP systems, letterheads are often used for generating printed documents like invoices, purchase orders, and statements."

